cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalisation, please cite the corresponding software release and the research paper when available."
type: software
title: "PlaneWave: formalised discretisation error bounds for Coulomb quantum simulation"
authors:
  - family-names: Berry
    given-names: Dominic W.
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
repository-code: "https://github.com/DominicWB/PlaneWave"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 and Mathlib formalisation accompanying the manuscript "Basis-set error
  bounds for first-quantised quantum simulation of chemistry". It covers plane-wave
  and spatial-grid error bounds for periodic Coulomb Hamiltonians: ground energies,
  smooth observables under the dynamics, logarithmic kinetic-energy bounds with
  stopping-power estimates, and the projection-flux and kinetic-energy-source
  estimates. For isolated systems it covers range-truncated free-boundary energy
  comparisons with the sufficient basis size, and dynamics and kinetic-energy
  bounds for Born-Oppenheimer and non-Born-Oppenheimer systems, including internal
  spin, under the stated regularity and localisation hypotheses.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - quantum simulation
  - first quantisation
  - Coulomb Hamiltonian
  - plane waves
  - basis-set error
